WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.160
The wild and wacky halls of Greendale&nbsp;
Community College have hosted a ton of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:09.540
big stars — and these are the ones who’ve&nbsp;
also gotten schwifty on "Rick and Morty."

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:15.480
Joel McHale played Jeff Winger, the de facto&nbsp;
leader of the main "Community" crew. A once&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:20.820
successful lawyer, his prestigious degree from&nbsp;
Columbia University is revealed to be a sham,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:25.380
forcing him out of his career. In a bid&nbsp;
to return to his high-profile lifestyle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:29.700
Winger enrolls at Greendale Community&nbsp;
College to receive a legitimate degree,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:35.520
where he becomes the leader of a colorful band&nbsp;
of misfits. After "Community" wrapped up in 2015,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:40.920
McHale went on to star in "The X-Files" and&nbsp;
even played former "Community" co-star Chevy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:47.040
Chase in the 2018 comedy "A Futile and Stupid&nbsp;
Gesture." However, he eventually reunited with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:52.260
his "Community" boss Dan Harmon for the "Rick and&nbsp;
Morty" Season 3 episode "Rickmancing the Stone."

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:56.400
In this episode, Rick transports&nbsp;
his grandchildren, Morty and Summer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:01.020
to a "Mad Max"-style universe filled&nbsp;
with chaos and vehicular warfare.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:05.280
McHale voiced the role of Hemorrhage,&nbsp;
the leader of a group that terrorizes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:10.320
the wastelands. Summer falls for Hemorrhage,&nbsp;
but their love story doesn't last long. Rick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:15.780
eventually helps the tribe become more civilized,&nbsp;
leading the macho Hemorrhage to adopt a simpler&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:20.700
and more docile way of life. Notably, Summer&nbsp;
isn't the only "Rick and Morty'' character to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:24.745
enjoy a brief romance with a character&nbsp;
voiced by a former "Community" star.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:30.120
In the "Rick and Morty" Season 5 episode "A&nbsp;
Rickconvenient Mort," Alison Brie voiced a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:35.340
fictional, eco-conscious superhero named&nbsp;
Planetina. While on an adventure with his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:40.140
grandfather, Morty encounters Planetina and&nbsp;
immediately falls for her. Surprisingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:44.580
the shy superhero also takes a liking to the&nbsp;
high schooler, and the two begin to date,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:49.620
much to the dismay of Morty's mother. After&nbsp;
hatching a plan to save Planetina from being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:54.480
sold to a rich sheik, the two spend their days&nbsp;
together saving the planet. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:59.100
Morty learns that Planetina places more&nbsp;
value in protecting the planet than she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:03.180
does in saving human lives, something that&nbsp;
forces the young man to break up with her.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:07.920
Brie rose to prominence after appearing&nbsp;
as the do-good, straight-A student Annie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:12.360
Edison in "Community." The youngest member&nbsp;
of the group, she often struggled to have her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:16.740
voice heard and was taken advantage of for her&nbsp;
proficiency in school. Throughout "Community,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:22.200
she shares a will-they-won't-they relationship&nbsp;
with Jeff Winger, which is ironic considering the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:26.340
two actors also both served as love interests&nbsp;
for different characters in "Rick and Morty."

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:30.120
The animated series doesn't seem too shy&nbsp;
about bringing back guest characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:33.960
and Planetina's story also wasn't&nbsp;
quite wrapped up entirely yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:39.549
so there's always the possibility that Brie's&nbsp;
character and Morty could reunite once again.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:44.820
"And now the elemental punch&nbsp;
that's too hot to handle. Wa-kah!"

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:49.740
Gillian Jacobs made quite the splash when&nbsp;
she joined "Community" as Britta Perry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:54.840
an activist struggling to find meaning in her&nbsp;
life through community college. Britta appeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:59.340
as a series regular in "Community" throughout&nbsp;
its six-season run. After the star wrapped up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:03.480
her time as Britta on the comedy, she went&nbsp;
on to appear in a number of Netflix series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:07.020
including Judd Apatow's "Love"&nbsp;
and the "Fear Street" trilogy.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:11.820
Jacobs has also spent the years since "Community"&nbsp;
ended lending her voice to animated characters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:17.400
After voicing characters in "Adventure Time,"&nbsp;
"American Dad!", and "Long Live the Royals,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:23.280
Jacobs briefly played an unhinged superhero in&nbsp;
"Rick and Morty." Jacobs appeared as Supernova&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:28.140
in the Season 3 episode "Vindicators 3:&nbsp;
The Return of Worldender." In the episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:33.840
a drunk Rick concocts a plan to terrorize a&nbsp;
team of prolific superheroes by putting them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:39.120
through life-ending challenges and puzzles that&nbsp;
take a page from the "Saw" franchise. After a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:43.620
number of trials and tribulations, Jacobs'&nbsp;
Supernova manages to make it out alive.

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:47.580
Despite surviving Rick's mayhem,&nbsp;
it remains to be seen whether&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:50.700
the character will ever return to&nbsp;
the series. Perhaps the character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:54.627
could even team up with Alison Brie's&nbsp;
Planetina at some point in the future?

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:59.520
After appearing in a recurring role as Dean&nbsp;
Pelton in the first 2 seasons of "Community,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:05.340
Jim Rash was promoted to a series regular in&nbsp;
Season 3. The fan-favorite character is best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:10.320
remembered for having a crush on Jeff and for&nbsp;
his many elaborate and sophisticated costumes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:16.260
While starring as the Dean of Greendale Community&nbsp;
College, Rash co-penned "The Descendants," which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:21.420
nabbed him a Best Adapted Screenplay award at&nbsp;
the Oscars. After "Community" called it a day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:24.360
the star quickly made a guest&nbsp;
appearance in "Rick and Morty."

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:29.760
The Oscar winner appeared in the Season 2&nbsp;
episode "Big Trouble in Little Sanchez" as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:34.620
Glaxlo Slimslom, an intergalactic marriage&nbsp;
counselor who tries to help Beth and Jerry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:40.140
reconcile their rocky relationship. Naturally,&nbsp;
not even the greatest marriage experts can tackle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:46.020
their marriage and chaos ensues. IGN praised the&nbsp;
episode and the Beth and Jerry storyline, writing:

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:48.900
"Between Jim Rash's guest&nbsp;
appearance and the wacky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:53.700
violent battle that ensued, the Beth/Jerry&nbsp;
storyline was unusually entertaining."

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:57.660
Seeing as Beth and Jerry's relationship&nbsp;
has evolved since the second season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:02.280
it seems unlikely that Rash will return&nbsp;
as the character anytime soon. The star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:06.000
more recently voiced a character in&nbsp;
"Solar Opposites," another animated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:09.890
series spearheaded by "Rick and&nbsp;
Morty" co-creator Justin Roiland.

00:05:10.034 --> 00:05:13.514
"You may already be learning something important."

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:17.460
Throughout its six-season run,&nbsp;
"Community" boasted a variety&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:22.140
of guest and regular appearances from&nbsp;
high-profile and established actors. A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:25.320
decent chunk of them have also popped up&nbsp;
in "Rick and Morty" throughout the years.

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:28.260
Perhaps the most obvious is Keith David,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:34.560
who appeared in the final season of "Community"&nbsp;
as Elroy Patashnik, a failed inventor. The actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:38.160
continues to occasionally appear as&nbsp;
President Curtis in "Rick and Morty."

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:43.380
John Oliver, who most people probably know as&nbsp;
the host of HBO's "Last Week Tonight," appeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:49.860
in "Community" as Ian Duncan, a psychology&nbsp;
professor at Greendale. In 2013, Oliver also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:55.320
voiced an amoeba named Dr. Xenon Bloom in the&nbsp;
"Rick and Morty" Season 1, episode "Anatomy Park."

00:05:55.320 --> 00:06:00.360
Nathan Fillion, who appeared as a Greendale&nbsp;
custodian in "Community," also showed up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:04.500
in "Rick and Morty" as a galactic secret&nbsp;
agent who wants access to Rick's formula&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:08.820
for interdimensional travel in the Season&nbsp;
3 episode "The Rickshank Rickdemption."

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:11.160
Seeing as "Rick and Morty" is still airing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:16.200
it remains to be seen if other cast members from&nbsp;
"Community" will appear in the animated sci-fi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:21.401
series. Perhaps "Community" series&nbsp;
regulars Danny Pudi, Donald Glover,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.401 --> 00:06:26.441
Yvette Nicole Brown, and Ken Jeong will get&nbsp;
their shots at voice roles in the show, too.

